body:
Applying the cache check to the nested if block does seem to resolve the problem, something like:
```cpp
if (array_mesh.is_valid()
	&& array_mesh->get_surface_count() > 0
	&& !wasCacheValid) {
	p_gizmo->add_mesh(array_mesh, material_arraymesh);
}
```
It appears as though the recreation of an `Instance` every time this code runs was the source of the problem, though I can't speak for what inside is actually causing that performance issue yet. I'm working on how to structure this to be less of a mess than the hack I've put together, but I'll get a PR in soon so it can be reviewed, even if this isn't the ideal approach, or a complete solution.
